73 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 46 0 R
/E (Educational institutions handle a large number of student requirements such as Form 137, birth certificates, valid IDs, report cards, and other enrollment documents. Managing these requirements manually can make it difficult to determine which students have already submitted their documents and which requirements are still incomplete. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
74 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 46 0 R
/E (Currently, staff may rely on spreadsheets, paper records, or separate files to monitor student submissions. This can result in duplicated records, delayed follow-ups, and difficulty generating accurate reports. The proposed Student Requirements and Document Tracking System is a web-based application that will allow authorized staff to digitally monitor student requirements, update submission status, and generate reports. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
75 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 46 0 R
/E (The system will centralize student requirement records and provide a clearer workflow for checking submitted, pending, and missing documents. It will also support reminders and reporting to help authorized personnel manage requirements more efficiently. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
76 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 46 0 R
/T (2. Purpose of the Project )
/E (2. Purpose of the Project )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
77 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 46 0 R
/E (This proposal aims to present a web-based application that will streamline the monitoring of student requirements, provide organized records of submitted and missing documents, and help authorized staff efficiently manage student compliance. The system is intended to reduce manual checking, improve record accuracy, and make requirement monitoring more accessible and organized. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
