/E (The Student Requirements and Document Tracking System is a web-based application designed to improve the management and monitoring of student requirements. The system addresses the difficulties of manually tracking documents such as Form 137, birth certificates, valid IDs, report cards, and other enrollment requirements. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [26]
>>
endobj
214 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 50 0 R
/E (It provides a centralized platform where authorized staff can manage student records and monitor the status of submitted, pending, and missing requirements. The system will include features such as user registration and login, role-based access, student record management, requirements checklists, submission status tracking, search and filtering, notifications or reminders, dashboards, and reports. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [27]
>>
endobj
215 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 50 0 R
/E (Administrators will be able to manage users, requirements, and system settings, while staff can update and monitor student records. Students can view their requirement status and identify missing or pending documents. Overall, the proposed system aims to reduce manual work, improve record organization and accuracy, simplify requirement monitoring, and make the process of managing student documents more efficient and accessible. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [28]
>>
